preConditionHook:
// EL: priorLow = lowest(low, lookback)[1], priorHigh = highest(high,
// lookback)[1] -- the extreme of the lookback bars ENDING ONE BAR AGO, so the
// reversal bar is compared against what it reversed and not against itself.
//
// Highest/Lowest bottom out in EL's Extremes(), which is EL SOURCE: seeded at
// the window's first bar, scanning the rest, STRICT comparison so a tie keeps
// the earliest bar. Being EL source, its relational operator carries the same
// 2.22e-12 tolerance every other EL comparison does, so the scan uses
// el_lt/el_gt rather than < and >. Written out as the loop it bottoms out in,
// the way Breakout and LargestTrendBarOfTheRun do.
priorLow = low[1];
priorHigh = high[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorLow)) priorLow = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorHigh)) priorHigh = high[i];
}
